From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Collins Ikechukwu <collinschristroa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:19:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] scf: count only browser events from a site's own domains

SCF_ENFORCE_ORIGIN makes /api/send require an Origin header that matches
the website's domain (or a subdomain; several domains may be listed,
comma-separated) and the Fetch Metadata headers browsers attach to fetch
calls. Plain server-side posts usually lack them.

Rejected events get the same reply as bots, and are counted per site,
reason and day in Redis (scf:rejected:*) for operator review.
